  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-08-09T12:39:20.719Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The avatar stealing and people using crashers/hacking programs is getting kinda high, its making a lot of people avoid public worlds unless they are a new player, then they soon also realize the issue and avoid public worlds if they have not quit the game already. \n\nThere is a reason why people joke about high ranked players staying in private worlds all the time, its because they dont want to be ddos, crashed, or have their work stolen when all their trying to do is have fun and make friends. \n\nCurrently the SDK already knows when you are uploading an avatar with someone else blueprint ID, it will bring an error saying it cant be uploaded. So it would be nice if in vrchat that worked the same way. That people cant use an avatar marked as private, which is how the private feature should be from the start. \n\n\nI know you guys say Security is one of your main focuses, so please find a way to stop all the hacking, ripping and crashing of players. So people dont have to hide in private worlds all the time and enjoy the game without being worried.",
